    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0OROUTC7",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 0, copy 7 of 10: same majority(A0, B0, C0) as T0OROUT, feeding T1H2N5C4.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_02a981298b174da38cbff01ecbf44228",
        "IdGuid": "0b77b0d7-8f0d-410d-9a5f-6cbc2b8897c2",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "b6603708-b01b-4432-9f1e-c0f7055c2270",
